.TH "rofimoji" "1" "2026\-08\-29" "Version 6.8.0" "Rofi Third\-party Add\-on Documentation"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
\fBrofimoji\fR \- An emoji and general character picker for rofi and rofi\-likes
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBrofimoji\fR [\fIOPTION\fR].\&.\&.\&
.PP
\fBrofimoji\fR \fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR
.PP
\fBrofimoji\fR \fB\-\-version\fR
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBrofimoji\fR is a character picker for \fBrofi\fR and other dmenu\-compatible
selectors (rofi\-likes).\& It allows the user to interactively search for
Unicode characters such as emoji by name or keyword, and then either
type the selected character into the currently focused window, copy it
to the clipboard, insert it via the clipboard, or print it to standard
output.\&
.PP
Characters are fuzzy\-searchable by keyword.\& Frequently and recently
used characters are remembered and presented first, unless disabled
with \fB\-\-no\-frecency\fR.\&
.PP
By default the bundled emoji set is shown, but any of the distributed
character files (or user\-provided files in
\fI${XDG_DATA_HOME}/rofimoji/data\fR) can be selected with \fB\-\-files\fR.\&
.PP
\fBrofimoji\fR can also be run as a \fBrofi\fR mode; see \fBrofimoji\-rofi\fR(7).\&
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB\-\-action\fR=\fIACTION\fR [\fIACTION\fR.\&.\&.\&], \fB\-a\fR \fIACTION\fR [\fIACTION\fR.\&.\&.\&]
.RS 4
How to insert the chosen character(s).\& More than one action may be
specified, space\-separated (e.\&g.\& \fB\-\-action type copy\fR).\& One of:
.PP
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fItype\fR: type the character(s) directly via the typer
.IP \(bu 4
\fIcopy\fR: copy the character(s) to the clipboard
.IP \(bu 4
\fIclipboard\fR: insert the character(s) indirectly via the clipboard
.IP \(bu 4
\fItype\-numerical\fR: type the Unicode codepoints via the compose key
.IP \(bu 4
\fIunicode\fR: type the Unicode codepoints of the character(s)
.IP \(bu 4
\fIcopy\-unicode\fR: copy the Unicode codepoints to the clipboard
.IP \(bu 4
\fIprint\fR: print the character(s) to standard output
.IP \(bu 4
\fImenu\fR: ask at selection time which action to perform
.PD
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-files\fR=\fIFILE\fR [\fIFILE\fR.\&.\&.\&], \fB\-f\fR \fIFILE\fR [\fIFILE\fR.\&.\&.\&]
.RS 4
Read characters from the given file(s), one entry per line.\&
\fIFILE\fR may be an absolute or relative path (globbing with asterisk
(*) is supported), or a bare name referring to one of the
distributed character files or any file in
\fI${XDG_DATA_HOME}/rofimoji/data\fR.\& The special value \fIall\fR selects
every distributed file at once.\&
.PP
In a config file, multiple files are written as a list, e.\&g.\&
\fIfiles = [emojis, math]\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-skin\-tone\fR=\fITONE\fR, \fB\-s\fR \fITONE\fR
.RS 4
Skin tone to use for all supporting emoji.\& One of: \fIneutral\fR,
\fIlight\fR, \fImedium\-light\fR, \fImoderate\fR, \fIdark brown\fR, \fIblack\fR, or
\fIask\fR.\& With \fIask\fR (the default), the user is prompted per emoji.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-max\-recent\fR=\fIN\fR
.RS 4
Show at most \fIN\fR recently used characters.\& \fIN\fR is capped at 10.\&
Set to 0 to disable the recent\-characters feature.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-frecency\fR
.RS 4
Do not sort characters by frequency\-of\-use.\& Characters appear in
the order they appear in the source file(s).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-only\-official\fR
.RS 4
Use only the official Unicode descriptions.\& Skip the additional
descriptions shipped with \fBrofimoji\fR and any user\-provided ones in
\fI${XDG_DATA_HOME}/rofimoji/data\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-hidden\-descriptions\fR
.RS 4
List only the characters, not their descriptions.\& Descriptions
remain searchable.\& Only meaningful for the \fIrofi\fR selector.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-use\-icons\fR
.RS 4
Render characters as icons in \fIrofi\fR.\& Not used by other selectors.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-prompt\fR=\fIPROMPT\fR, \fB\-r\fR \fIPROMPT\fR
.RS 4
Set the prompt text shown by the selector.\& Default is "😀 ".\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-selector\fR=\fISELECTOR\fR
.RS 4
Use \fISELECTOR\fR as the selection dialog instead of the
auto\-detected default.\& One of: \fIrofi\fR, \fIwofi\fR, \fIfuzzel\fR, \fIbemenu\fR,
\fItofi\fR, \fIdmenu\fR, \fIwmenu\fR, \fIchoose\fR, \fIhyprlauncher\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-selector\-args\fR=\fIARGS\fR
.RS 4
A string of arguments passed through to the selector.\& Quoting
matters; prefer \fI\-\-selector\-args="ARGS"\fR or
\fI\-\-selector\-args " ARGS"\fR due to an argparse limitation
(https://bugs.\&python.\&org/issue9334).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-clipboarder\fR=\fICLIPBOARDER\fR
.RS 4
Use \fICLIPBOARDER\fR to access the clipboard.\& One of: \fIxsel\fR,
\fIxclip\fR, \fIwl\-copy\fR, \fIpbcopy\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-typer\fR=\fITYPER\fR
.RS 4
Use \fITYPER\fR to type characters.\& One of: \fIxdotool\fR, \fIwtype\fR,
\fIydotool\fR, \fIcliclick\fR, \fIwl\-ime\-type\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-keybinding\-copy\fR=\fIKEY\fR
\fB\-\-keybinding\-type\fR=\fIKEY\fR
\fB\-\-keybinding\-clipboard\fR=\fIKEY\fR
\fB\-\-keybinding\-type\-numerical\fR=\fIKEY\fR
\fB\-\-keybinding\-unicode\fR=\fIKEY\fR
\fB\-\-keybinding\-copy\-unicode\fR=\fIKEY\fR
.RS 4
Override the default keybinding for the copy, type, clipboard,
type\-numerical, unicode, and copy\-unicode actions respectively.\&
Defaults: \fIAlt+c\fR, \fIAlt+t\fR, \fIAlt+p\fR, \fIAlt+n\fR, \fIAlt+u\fR, \fIAlt+i\fR.\&
Effective with the \fIrofi\fR and \fIfuzzel\fR selectors; see \fIKEYBINDINGS\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Print brief usage information and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-version\fR
.RS 4
Print the version number and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.PP
Custom keybindings are supported by the \fIrofi\fR and \fIfuzzel\fR selectors.\&
All other selectors (\fIwofi\fR, \fIbemenu\fR, \fItofi\fR, \fIdmenu\fR, \fIwmenu\fR,
\fIchoose\fR, \fIhyprlauncher\fR) ignore the \fB\-\-keybinding\-*\fR options and only
provide the default \fIEnter\fR confirmation.\&
.PP
With \fIrofi\fR or \fIfuzzel\fR, the following keybindings are active (defaults
shown; configurable via the \fB\-\-keybinding\-*\fR options):
.PP
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fIEnter\fR: perform the default action (see \fB\-\-action\fR)
.IP \(bu 4
\fIShift+Enter\fR: select multiple characters
.IP \(bu 4
\fIAlt+c\fR: copy the selected character(s) to the clipboard
.IP \(bu 4
\fIAlt+t\fR: type the selected character(s) directly
.IP \(bu 4
\fIAlt+p\fR: insert the selected character(s) via the clipboard
.IP \(bu 4
\fIAlt+n\fR: type the Unicode codepoint(s) numerically
(Ctrl+Shift+U.\&.\&.\&)
.IP \(bu 4
\fIAlt+u\fR: type the Unicode codepoint(s) of the selection
.IP \(bu 4
\fIAlt+i\fR: copy the Unicode codepoint(s) of the selection to
the clipboard
.PD
.PP
Additionally, \fIrofi\fR provides shortcuts to insert recently used
characters via \fIAlt+1\fR, \fIAlt+2\fR, etc.\& (inserting the Nth\-most\-recently
used character).\& These use rofi'\&s built\-in keybindings and are not
configurable through \fBrofimoji\fR.\& This feature is \fIrofi\fR\-only; \fIfuzzel\fR
does not provide an equivalent.\&
.PP
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
\fB0\fR
.RS 4
Success.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB1\fR
.RS 4
A runtime error occurred (e.\&g.\& no selector found, no typer
available, configuration error).\&
.PP
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.PP
\fIXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR
.RS 4
Base directory for the \fIrofimoji.\&rc\fR config file.\& Defaults to
\fI\(ti/.\&config\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fIXDG_CONFIG_DIRS\fR
.RS 4
Colon\-separated list of system config directories searched for
\fIrofimoji.\&rc\fR.\& Defaults to \fI/etc/xdg\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fIXDG_DATA_HOME\fR
.RS 4
Base directory for user character data, the \fIrecent\fR and
\fIfrecency\fR files.\& Defaults to \fI\(ti/.\&local/share\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fIXDG_CACHE_HOME\fR
.RS 4
Base directory for the \fBrofimoji\fR cache.\& Defaults to \fI\(ti/.\&cache\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH FILES
.PP
\fI\(ti/.\&config/rofimoji.\&rc\fR
.RS 4
Per\-user configuration file.\& Long option names without leading
dashes are used as keys; see \fICONFIGURATION\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fI/etc/xdg/rofimoji.\&rc\fR
.RS 4
System\-wide configuration file.\& Searched via \fI$XDG_CONFIG_DIRS\fR
(default \fI/etc/xdg\fR); each directory in that colon\-separated list
is checked.\&
.PP
.RE
\fI\(ti/.\&local/share/rofimoji/recent\fR
.RS 4
Stores the recently used characters.\&
.PP
.RE
\fI\(ti/.\&local/share/rofimoji/frecency\fR
.RS 4
Stores the frequency\-of\-use data used to order characters when
\fB\-\-no\-frecency\fR is not set.\&
.PP
.RE
\fI\(ti/.\&local/share/rofimoji/data/filename.\&additional.\&csv\fR
.RS 4
Additional characters or additional descriptions for the character
set in \fIfilename\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
Options starting with \fI\-\-\fR can also be set in a config file.\& The config
file syntax allows:
.PP
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fIkey = value\fR for options taking a value
.IP \(bu 4
\fIflag = true\fR for boolean options
.IP \(bu 4
\fIkey = [a, b, c]\fR for list\-valued options
.PD
.PP
For example:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
action = copy
files = [emojis, math]
skin\-tone = moderate
.fi
.RE
.PP
If an option is specified in more than one place, command\-line values
override values from the config file.\& See
https://github.\&com/fdw/rofimoji#example\-config\-file for further
details.\&
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run with defaults (emoji, type on selection):
.RS 4
$ rofimoji
.RE
Copy instead of type, using math symbols in addition to emoji:
.RS 4
$ rofimoji \-\-action copy \-\-files emojis,math
.RE
Use \fIfuzzel\fR as the selector and \fIwl\-copy\fR for clipboard:
.RS 4
$ rofimoji \-\-selector fuzzel \-\-clipboarder wl\-copy
.RE
